  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 306 AM EST Thu Nov 26 2026\n\nCurrent system will be pulling out of the area by Friday evening to \nstart the long term forecast. Cold air will pour into the area and \nclouds will come to an end, bringing temperatures overnight down \ninto the 20s and 30s. Aloft, another system will be loading up right \nbehind this one, which will quickly turn winds on Saturday back to \nthe south to southwest allowing us to warm back up into the upper \n50s to 60s across north and central Georgia. \n\nStrong PV anomaly digs into the the Great Plains early Sunday and\ncombines with a sheared bit of the previous, exiting system \nacross Texas and Mexico to bring moisture surging back into the \narea. Whether or not this can turn into some decent rainfall \nremains a question, as ensembles are a bit mixed. Euro ensemble is\na bit more aggressive in rainfall thanks to a slightly more \nvigorous wave (and possibly some model physics, but I digress) \ncompared to others. For now, confident in seeing some rainfall \nacross Sunday evening possibly into early Monday morning likely \nahead of a front moving into the area. This front won't be very \nstrong, so temperatures remain in the 50s and 60s and remain so \nwith slight warming into the middle of the week next week.",
